A||||5||HummelHund||Fire Breathing Duke||||1||
Z||000000||HummelHund||05-04-2001||01:52 PM||||Well, I started up my '84 SE today and noticed a strange phenomena, smoke coming out of the intake vent thingy on the rear fender. I know I'm having problems with oil in my air cleaner and I know what can be causing that (thanks 85Josh), but shouldn't the smoke be sucked in to the intake instead of coming out?  I do have some smoke in my air cleaner due to the oil in there, but still, isn't this weird? What's wrong with my poor Fiero?<BR>Thanks<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6 (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe ($150 running car)||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||05-04-2001||05:17 PM|||| That's weird! What color was the smoke and when does it happen (cold/ hot engine). Does it go away after a while?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rex||05-04-2001||05:39 PM||||Is the engine backfiring? That could be one source of smoke.||||reg||1
Z||000003||HummelHund||05-04-2001||06:08 PM||||The smoke is a sort of light grey, the same color as the smoke in my air cleaner and the same as the smoke coming out of my breather filter. It doesn't take it long to start smoking, maybe a couple of minutes. I haven't run the engine for a very long time, but from what I can tell it doesn't really go away. The engine doesn't backfire, I'm pretty sure the smoke is coming from the breather filter, but wouldn't it stay in the air cleaner portion of the assembly, instead of coming out the intake? I would think the engine would suck the smoke toward the throttle body. I'm going to replace the breather filter (I think it's the original, and it's looking pretty bad) to see if that helps any. Oh and by the way, NEVER use Deutsch breather filters. They don't fit. Buy AC Delco. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6 (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe ($150 running car)||||reg||1
Z||000004||HummelHund||05-04-2001||07:27 PM||||OK, I feel stupid. I remebered that when I was watching the car smoke that I had the top of the air cleaner off. I put it back on, no smoke. The TBI was getting its air from the huge open air cleaner instead of from the intake, allowing the smoke to escape out the intake. I'll be putting on my dunce cap now. B)<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6 (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe ($150 running car)||||reg||1
Z||000005||84Bill||05-04-2001||11:00 PM||||Hehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> gonna say all ya need now is a disco ball and some of those neon lights under the car..<P>Replace the PCV valve and brether filter if she still works up a lather in the cleaner then I'm sad to say yet another duke down... rings my friend rings... nothing short of an overhaul will bring ole duke back from the edge.||||reg||10
